& [Solution]
  + a new cantor_sop_semantics crate owns strict serializable semantic forms and an effect-free analysis pipeline
  + deterministic normalization and domain-separated hashing produce replayable document and generation identities
  + bounded validators preserve dependency subject field role relation expression view and exact-span invariants
  + a source analyzer returns diagnostics plus a partial semantic document without reading files or contacting any service
  + strict deserialization rejects unknown fields and duplicate semantic-set members instead of silently erasing them
  + an independent custody verifier binds every adapted module to the recorded live-source bytes

& [ComponentBoundary]
  + promoted capability kernel.sop.semantic-analyze is implemented by the bounded crate
  + the published instance contract remains the authority boundary for later instance composition
  + cantor_scribe remains a held whole-crate candidate; no storage service or transport is promoted by association

& [EffectBoundary]
  + all operations receive supplied strings or in-memory forms and return values or bounded faults
  + no filesystem process environment database async network provider CLI unsafe installation update mutation publication or model-inference path exists

& [VerifiedBoundary]
